    "user_request_original": "Design a 29-layer planar dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Materials are Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) in alternating sequence starting with Ta2O5 (Gao) at the air interface. Layers 1-9 and 21-29 (outer Bragg mirrors) have fixed thicknesses: Ta2O5 (Gao) layers at 185 nm, SiO2 (Lemarchand) layers at 267 nm (quarter-wave optical thickness at 1550 nm based on recalled indices). Layers 10-20 (11 central cavity layers) have optimizable thicknesses bounded between 50 nm and 400 nm. Optimize for maximum mean transmittance at 1550 nm (single wavelength target) and minimum mean transmittance across 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Use coherent transfer-matrix method solver. Total layer count is exactly 29.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Design a 29-layer planar dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence using alternating Ta2O5 and SiO2 layers. Layers 1-9 and 21-29 have fixed thicknesses (185 nm for Ta2O5, 267 nm for SiO2). Layers 10-20 are optimizable between 50 nm and 400 nm. Optimize for maximum mean transmittance at 1550 nm and minimum mean transmittance across 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands using coherent TMM.",
